 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You've been crawling for twenty minutes. Then the road just opens up.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 101
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "No crash. No roadworks. Nothing.",
   "from": 104,
   "to": 158
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You floor it, sure you've beaten the traffic.",
   "from": 161,
   "to": 208
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "At the rest stop, you sip your coffee like a genius.",
   "from": 212,
   "to": 292
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then the trucker from behind you walks in, shaking her head.",
   "from": 296,
   "to": 379
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "trucker",
   "text": "There was no crash, honey. It was just us, braking.",
   "from": 395,
   "to": 483
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Sounds crazy, but scientists in Japan tested it.",
   "from": 486,
   "to": 553
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In a twenty oh eight study, they put twenty-two cars on a circular track.",
   "from": 556,
   "to": 666
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The loop was two hundred thirty metres. No obstacle at all.",
   "from": 670,
   "to": 767
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Every driver got one rule: cruise at thirty, follow safely.",
   "from": 771,
   "to": 872
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "At first, the circle flowed perfectly.",
   "from": 876,
   "to": 950
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then tiny wobbles appeared in the gaps.",
   "from": 954,
   "to": 1009
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "One car slowed a little. The one behind slowed more.",
   "from": 1013,
   "to": 1087
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Soon, cars were stopping completely.",
   "from": 1091,
   "to": 1142
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A stop-and-go wave was born. Here's the weird part.",
   "from": 1146,
   "to": 1223
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The cars drive forward, but the jam crawls backward, about twenty kilometres an hour.",
   "from": 1227,
   "to": 1348
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "New cars join its back as others leave its front.",
   "from": 1352,
   "to": 1418
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Bottlenecks still cause jams, by packing cars closer.",
   "from": 1421,
   "to": 1511
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But packed tightly enough, one tap of the brakes is all it takes.",
   "from": 1515,
   "to": 1600
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Back on the highway, the wave is still rolling backward.",
   "from": 1604,
   "to": 1676
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Twenty minutes behind you, someone is looking for a crash.",
   "from": 1679,
   "to": 1745
  }
 ],
